covered because the vertical line \\(x=1\\) is *not* present, but each such point also satisfies \\(b\\le n\\) and therefore belongs to the set \\(S_n\\) with \\(a+b\\le n+1\\); the equality \\(b\\le n\\) guarantees that \\((1,b)\\) lies on the line \\(y=x\\) after adding the vertical line \\(x=b\\) which is present when \\(b\\ge 2\\). Consequently every point of \\(S_n\\) is covered, and exactly one line (\\(y=x\\)) is sunny.\n\n   All three values of \\(k\\) are therefore attainable.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{k\\in\\{0,1,n\\}}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
